ute mark-submitted <file> [--issue-url <url>]`, or `pose contribute dismiss <file>`.\n-- Check contributor status: `pose contribute status`\n-- Stage a contribution manually: `pose contribute stage --type <bug|enhancement> --title <title>`\n-- Disable contributor mode: `pose contribute disable`\n-- Privacy guarantee: staged reports strictly isolate POSE engine mechanics and never leak proprietary code.\n ## Opt-in progressive review profiles (ABM)\n \n Add `engineering-judgment@1` and/or `high-criticality-review@1` explicitly to\n   252\t`pose validate --carry` refreshes the canonical structured result. It runs the modules the changed-scope rules select since the canonical base and carries the other checks with their outcome and the head where they ran. The changed set ignores the result file and the derived administrative records that material bindings already ignore. Any doubt about the base runs everything, and the record says why. Modules can declare `selfContained` to stop being widened by changes outside every module. The delivery index reads a carried result as an observation of its own head. The record now names the engine version together with its build revision.\n   253\t\n   254\t### Files and modules changed\n   255\t`pose-mcp/internal/cli` (validate, its scope selection, its result fields and the help catalogue), `pose-mcp/internal/pose` (the delivery reading of the result), the manual in English and pt-BR with their embedded copies, this spec and its ADR.\n   256\t\n   257\t### Validation executed\n   258\tSee the execution log: the package tests with mutation checks, the full `go test ./...` and the strict matrix with 236 of 236 checks.\n   259\t\n   260\t### Residual risks\n   261\tAn instance that declares a module self-contained while its checks read files outside it would carry a stale result. The declaration is explicit and documented, and the default stays the full fallback.\n   262\t\n   263\t### Follow-ups\n   264\t- [open] F1: cover with an end-to-end test that a review bundle sealed over a carried record judges the carried head (seal, verify and closeout-check on a fixture). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n   265\t- [open] F2: `--carry --report` lists carried checks as executed commands without their `carried_from` head and time; exclude them from the executed summary and label reused results (review round 13, N39). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-15)\n   190\t\t}\n   191\t\tif caseInsensitiveFilesystem(root, os.Stat) {\n   192\t\t\treturn unused(\"the filesystem is case-insensitive, so changes cannot be attributed to modules\")\n   193\t\t}\n   194\t\t// A case-folded directory inside a case-sensitive filesystem is an alias\n   195\t\t// too (review round 8, N22).\n   196\t\tfor _, dir := range carryRelevantDirs(root, modules, meta) {\n   197\t\t\tif casefoldedDirectory(dir, os.ReadDir, os.Lstat) {\n   198\t\t\t\treturn unused(\"directory %s folds case, so changes cannot be attributed to modules\", dir)\n   199\t\t\t}\n   200\t\t}\n   201\t\t// Check ids must be unique: two checks sharing an id would share one base\n   202\t\t// result (review round 7, N19).\n   203\t\tif id := duplicateCheckID(matrix, modules); id != \"\" {\n   204\t\t\treturn unused(\"the matrix defines check %s more than once\", id)\n   205\t\t}\n   206\t\tbaseIDs := map[string]bool{}\n   207\t\tfor _, check := range base.Checks {\n   208\t\t\tif baseIDs[check.ID] {\n   209\t\t\t\treturn unused(\"the canonical result records check %s more than once\", check.ID)\n   210\t\t\t}\n   211\t\t\tbaseIDs[check.ID] = true\n   212\t\t}\n   213\t\tif err := posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", base.GitHead, head).Run(); err != nil {\n   214\t\t\treturn unused(\"the canonical result's head %s is not an ancestor of HEAD\", base.GitHead)\n   215\t\t}\n   216\t\tselection, err := computeChangedScopeWith(root, base.GitHead, head, modules, meta, carryExclusions(root, base.GitHead, head, resultsPath)...)\n   217\t\tif err != nil {\n   218\t\t\treturn unused(\"changed-scope selection failed: %v\", err)\n   219\t\t}\n   220\t\tplan.base = map[string]checkResult{}\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:4:// comparable canonical result as base, validate --carry runs the modules the\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:26:// carryRecord is the run's account of its base (R5).\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:27:type carryRecord struct {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:35:// carryPlan is what a usable base lets the run reuse.\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:36:type carryPlan struct {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:37:\trecord    *carryRecord\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:45:func (p carryPlan) carried(module string) bool {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:55:func (p carryPlan) carriedResult(id string) checkResult {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:65:func planCarry(root, resultsPath, mode, matrixSHA, head string, matrix validationMatrix, modules []validationModule) carryPlan {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:66:\tplan := carryPlan{record: &carryRecord{}}\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:68:\tunused := func(format string, args ...any) carryPlan {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:125:\t// alias form (review rounds 4–7, N9, N13, N16–N18), a carry needs a\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:196:\tfor _, dir := range carryRelevantDirs(root, modules, meta) {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:216:\tselection, err := computeChangedScopeWith(root, base.GitHead, head, modules, meta, carryExclusions(root, base.GitHead, head, resultsPath)...)\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:236:\t\t\t\tselection.Selected[module.Rel] = \"carry: no prior result for \" + id\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:246:// carryExclusions are the changed paths that are not changes for the carry\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:251:func carryExclusions(root, base, head, resultsPath string) []string {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:481:// carryRelevantDirs are the directories whose case behaviour decides whether\npose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:485:func carryRelevantDirs(root string, modules []validationModule, meta scopeMetadata) []string {\n17:      \"rationale\": \"Examined R2 and the start/end cleanliness, reflog and cancellation witnesses. An unavailable binding alone no longer invalidates a clean base; unclean or cancelled runs clear material_clean and invalidate bindings. Verified the relevant focused tests. Correct selfContained declarations remain an explicit instance-owned assumption, documented in the spec and manual.\"\n22:      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/validate-concurrent-steps-integration\",\n114:      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n116:      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n120:      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n164:      \"id\": \"validate\",\n170:      \"id\": \"validate\",\n183:    \"integration:pose-mcp/go/validate-concurrent-steps-integration\",\n191:      \"evidence\": \"file:pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623\",\n201:      \"evidence\": \"file:.pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:261\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
