erage remains N61.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Skipped the writing assessment. Manually scanned added implementation lines for TODO, FIXME, stub and panic markers and checked the spec's owned follow-ups; no new marker debt was established.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion requires the recorded and verified review conclusion. No attestation or closeout was recorded in this review execution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until POSE records this conclusion; it cannot establish the validity of an attestation that does not yet exist.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully and applied the selected Backend Go, security and documentation rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposition relies on the supplied sealed canonical validation run, which contains passing build, unit, integration and e2e evidence. Did not rerun the writing full matrix in this read-only checkout. Independently ran focused tests, vet and selected race tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the supplied sealed pose-mcp validation evidence. Independently passed focused CLI tests, the delivery parser test, scoped vet and selected race tests. The full --strict --module pose-mcp command was not rerun because it may write checkout artifacts.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"N60\",\n    \"N61\",\n    \"delegated-run:rrn-41f73b6e7465d0bb\",\n    \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adversarial-corpus\",\n    \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n}\n\n// dispatchValidationEntries starts the entries in matrix order, up to jobs at\n// a time; an exclusive check waits for the running ones and runs alone (spec\n// pose-validate-concurrent-steps R1–R2). A cancelled run starts nothing more.\nfunc dispatchValidationEntries(ctx context.Context, entries []*validationEntry, jobs int, matrix validationMatrix) {\n\tslots := make(chan struct{}, jobs)\n\tvar running sync.WaitGroup\n\tcancelled := func(entry *validationEntry) bool {\n\t\tif ctx.Err() == nil {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t\tentry.markCancelled()\n\t\tclose(entry.done)\n\t\treturn true\n\t}\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif entry.note != \"\" || entry.silent || entry.isolated {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif entry.check.Exclusive {\n\t\t\trunning.Wait()\n\t\t\tif cancelled(entry) {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif entry.resolveWhen(); entry.skip == \"\" {\n\t\t\t\tentry.execute(ctx, matrix, false, nil, nil, nil)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tclose(entry.done)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tselect {\n\t\tcase slots <- struct{}{}:\n\t\tcase <-ctx.Done():\n\t\t\tcancelled(entry)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif cancelled(entry) {\n\t\t\t<-slots\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\trunning.Add(1)\n\t\tgo func(entry *validationEntry) {\n\t\t\tdefer running.Done()\n\t\t\tdefer func() { <-slots }()\n\t\t\tif entry.resolveWhen(); entry.skip == \"\" {\n\t\t\t\tentry.execute(ctx, matrix, false, nil, nil, nil)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tclose(entry.done)\n\t\t}(entry)\n\t}\n}\n\n// validationResources is what a run may use. memoryKnown separates an empty\n// reading from none; unresolved says a cgroup applies whose limits could not\n// be located.\n\t\tif check.Outcome == \"error\" {\n\t\t\tseverity = \"error\"\n\t\t}\n\t\tusageFindings = append(usageFindings, usageFinding{ID: check.ID, Severity: severity})\n\t}\n\tnoteUsageFindings(stdout, result, usageFindings, true)\n\tfor name, writer := range map[string]struct {\n\t\tpath  string\n\t\twrite func(string, validationRunResult) error\n\t}{\n\t\t\"json\":  {jsonOut, writeValidationJSON},\n\t\t\"junit\": {junitOut, writeValidationJUnit},\n\t\t\"sarif\": {sarifOut, writeValidationSARIF},\n\t} {\n\t\tif writer.path == \"\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\ttarget := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(writer.path))\n\t\tif name == \"json\" && canonicalResultsPath != \"\" && normalizeValidationOutputPath(writer.path) == canonicalResultsPath {\n\t\t\terr := publishCanonicalValidationJSONIn(store, writer.path, canonicalResultsPath, run)\n\t\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\t\tif errors.Is(err, posemodel.ErrPublishUnsynced) {\n\t\t\t\t\tout := render(stdout, stderr)\n\t\t\t\t\tout.ContractLine(fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: %s\", name, target))\n\t\t\t\t\tout.Finding(cliout.Finding{State: cliout.StateWarning, Code: \"validation-result-durability\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\tMessage: fmt.Sprintf(\"%s result was published but durability is unconfirmed: %v\", name, err)})\n\t\t\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\trender(io.Discard, stderr).Failure(fmt.Sprintf(cliText(locale, \"writing %s result: %v\", \"escrevendo resultado %s: %v\"), name, err))\n\t\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\trender(stdout, stderr).ContractLine(fmt.Sprintf(\"%s: %s\", name, target))\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(target), 0o755); err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: creating %s result directory: %v\\n\", \"Erro: criando diretório do resultado %s: %v\\n\"), name, err)\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := writer.write(target, run); err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: writing %s result: %v\\n\", \"Erro: escrevendo resultado %s: %v\\n\"), name, err)\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"%s: %s\\n\", name, target)\n\t}\n\tif planOut != \"\" {\n\t\tdigest := sha256.Sum256(raw)\n\t\thead := \"\"\n\t\tif out, err := posemodel.RawHistoryGit(root, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\").Output(); err == nil {\n\t\t\thead = strings.TrimSpace(string(out))\n\t\t}\n\t\tplan := executionPlan{\n\t\t\tSchemaVersion: validationResultSchema,\n\t\t\tGeneratedAt:   run.GeneratedAt,\n\t\t\tProjectID:     posemodel.DefaultProjectID(root),\n\t\t\tSpec:          reportTask,\n\t\t\tGitHead:       head,\n\t\t\tMatrixSHA256:  hex.EncodeToString(digest[:]),\n\t\t\tChecks:        isolationChecks,\n\t\t\tApproval:      planApproval{Required: true},\n\t\t}\n\t\tif plan.Checks == nil {\n\t\t\tplan.Checks = []checkResult{}\n\t\t}\n\t\ttarget := filepath.Join(root, filepath.FromSlash(planOut))\n\t\tif err := writeExecutionPlan(target, plan); err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, cliText(locale, \"Error: writing execution plan: %v\\n\", \"Erro: escrevendo plano de execução: %v\\n\"), err)\n\t\t\treturn 1\n\t\t}\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"plan: %s (%d isolated check(s); approval required before Harness execution)\\n\", target, len(plan.Checks))\n\t}\n\tif autoReport {\n\t\tif reportTask == \"\" {\n\t\t\treportTask = \"validate-native\"\n\t\t}\n\t\treportArgs := []string{\"--task\", reportTask, \"--context\", \"auto-validate\", \"--validation-profile\", mode}\n\t\t// The outcome travels inside the summary, so it stays derived rather\n\t\t// than being recorded as a manual assertion.\n\t\t_ = runReportWith(root, reportArgs, nil, validationSummaryOf(run), io.Discard, stderr)\n\t}\n\tif failures > 0 {\n\t\treturn 1\n\t}\n\treturn 0\n}\n\n// validationSummaryOf projects a finished run for `pose report`: the commands\n// it executed and one line per check, with the outcome the run reached. It is\n// the structured replacement for parsing the printed output (spec\n// pose-cli-output-rendering-system R5).\npose-mcp/internal/cli/surface_check.go:189:func cmdSurfaceCheck(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\npose-mcp/internal/cli/artifact_integrity.go:787:func cmdArtifactCheck(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
