changed results with their actual origin supplies a complete record without claiming a new observation. D2 makes matrix and engine changes rerun everything; D3 makes narrower root-change behavior explicit. The dirty-base regression fixture directly tests the cheapest invalid reuse path.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-253b523c\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR records the canonical carry design and preservation of original check provenance required by D1, whose declared basis is R3, R4 and R7. It also documents comparability and the opt-in selfContained trade-off.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the help entry, English and Portuguese manual changes and both scaffold copies with runtime eligibility and selection behavior. All four manuals now explain that an uncomputable material binding alone does not refuse a base. The English instance-only Contributor Mode section explains the unrelated full-file scaffold difference.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N60\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fallback reasons and selection explanations are actionable; the remaining report provenance defect is accepted as the existing low-severity F2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N61\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Mapped R1-R10 to implementation and focused tests. Direct R7 parsing coverage passed, but the additional end-to-end delivery-consumer assurance remains the explicitly owned F1 gap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The declared runtime paths, tests, manuals, help and ADR implement the approved carry scope. The unavailable-binding change matches the current R2 wording. Administrative review artifacts were distinguished from the implementation under review.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adversarial-corpus\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined revision confinement before Git calls, dependency containment, symlink and case alias refusals, hidden index entries, submodule state and administrative exclusions. Focused negative tests passed. Carry relies on the existing local validation-record authority boundary and does not introduce external execution authority.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The implementation reuses changed-scope selection and compares the whole matrix and engine rather than introducing a per-command cache or arbitrary input hashing. Rejecting every unavailable spec binding would unnecessarily disable reuse; the independent material_clean witness addresses the actual dirty-base cause. The choice becomes insufficient if checks read undeclared inputs outside their module and dependencies.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
