{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: approved\n\nNo blocking defect found. Two existing low-priority follow-ups remain accepted: report provenance and dedicated end-to-end coverage for carried records.\n\nFocused CLI tests, the delivery-parser test, scoped `go vet`, and selected race tests passed. Explicit-range artifact reconciliation exited 0 with warnings only. Surface-check passed with one target, 236 results, and zero findings. Full validation relies on the supplied sealed evidence; I did not rerun commands that could modify checkout artifacts.\n\nApplied the review workflow and Backend Go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. Reviewed bundle `rvb-3540657ae0a94c2f`, digest `sha256:3540657ae0a94c2f7019d7642aa90f2738f393f23311d03089e32ba565262504`. HEAD remained `481d36dfd2ea673b5f5dc58a76d3e4213dac35bf`, and the working tree remained clean. No attestation was recorded.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N62\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1623,\n      \"summary\": \"Existing F2 remains: validationSummaryOf includes carried checks in executed Commands and renders their previous outcomes and durations without their original head or time. A newly dated --carry --report therefore presents reused observations as commands executed by this run.\",\n      \"action\": \"Complete spec follow-up F2: exclude carried checks from executed Commands and label reused results with carried_from and carried_generated_at.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N63\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md\",\n      \"line\": 264,\n      \"summary\": \"Existing F1 remains: direct delivery-reader coverage verifies carried head and time, but no dedicated end-to-end fixture seals a bundle, verifies it and checks closeout over a carried record.\",\n      \"action\": \"Complete spec follow-up F1 with a fixture proving seal, verify and closeout-check judge the carried check's original head.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-15\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R12-N39\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R13-N42\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R14-N44\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R16-N51\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R17-N53\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R17-N54\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Spec line 264 retains F1. go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose -run TestDeliveryValidationRunReadsTheCarriedHead -count=1 passed, but this test exercises parsing rather than seal, verify and closeout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R18-N55\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R18-N56\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Spec line 264 retains F1. The direct carried-head parser test passed; no dedicated carried-record seal/verify/closeout fixture was found in the reviewed tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R19-N60\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1623-1636 still includes carried commands and omits their origin; owned as F2 at spec line 265.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R19-N61\",\n      \"status\": \"not-fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Spec line 264 retains F1. The direct carried-head parser test passed; the dedicated end-to-end consumer journey remains absent.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the requested dec2e64c1395fafbf8e2a78171e5437c1720bbbf..481d36dfd2ea673b5f5dc58a76d3e4213dac35bf source diff, requirements R1-R10, decisions D1-D3, ADR, CLI help, English and Portuguese manuals and scaffold copies. Swept eligibility, unavailable bindings, cleanliness and reflog witnesses, cancellation, hidden index entries, submodule and alias handling, pinned metadata, changed-scope ownership and dependency widening, base completeness, chained provenance, failure accounting, dispatch, serialization, report projection and delivery consumption. Examined negative tests, the adversarial corpus and owned follow-ups. Focused CLI tests, direct delivery-parser test, scoped vet and selected race tests passed. Explicit-range artifact-check exited 0 with warning-only findings; surface-check exited 0 with zero findings. Full matrix evidence was supplied by the sealed bundle, not rerun. Final git status was clean. No blocker beyond the two accepted existing low-priority follow-ups was established.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined R2 and the start/end full cleanliness predicate, movement witnesses and cancellation invalidation. Removing the unavailable-binding refusal leaves material_clean as the independent witness that the base validated its head; unclean or cancelled runs invalidate bindings. Focused tests passed. Correct selfContained declarations remain an explicit instance-owned assumption; arbitrary undeclared check inputs are outside the design's guarantee.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/validate-concurrent-steps-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Carried entries are silent and bypass dispatch; aggregation reads their unchanged results. Traced cancellation finalization and lifecycle behavior. Focused Validate tests and selected race tests for cancellation, cancelled bases and submodule movement passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed additive result fields and legacy fallback behavior. The delivery reader preserves run-level provenance for ordinary records and uses per-check provenance for carried records. The direct carried-head and time parser test passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Focused tests passed for incompatible flags, unusable bases, malformed or unreadable metadata, path aliases, hidden index entries and cancellation. Invalid eligibility widens to full execution with a reason; incompatible invocation flags return exit 2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N63\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The producer-to-delivery-reader boundary is directly tested. Dedicated carried-record seal, verify and closeout coverage remains the accepted low-priority F1 gap.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N62\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Structured provenance, carry counts and fallback explanations are present, but the human report summary still loses carried provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined CLI parsing, schema additions and the delivery consumer. Carry is opt-in, old records retain their meaning, and records without engine_version cannot become carry bases. The selfContained extension is specified and documented.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independently passed go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/cli -run 'Carry|ChangedScope|Validate|Material|Cancellation' -count=1 and the direct delivery-parser test. Examined selection, chained origins, preserved failures, missing prior results and cleanliness invalidation. Full build and matrix coverage relies on the supplied sealed evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"D1 addresses the inability of partial changed-scope records to replace canonical evidence: a complete result retains each reused observation's actual origin. D2 conservatively rejects matrix or engine changes; D3 makes narrower root-change behavior explicit. The cheapest stale-reuse shortcut is representing an old observation as newly executed; carried_from and the delivery reader preserve its origin, and dirty-base tests reject invalid reuse. The corpus has no dedicated carried-record seal/closeout case; N63 records that assurance gap.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-253b523c\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR records canonical carry and original-observation provenance required by D1, whose declared basis is R3, R4 and R7. It also records the D2 comparability boundary and D3 selfContained trade-off.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared help, both language manuals and scaffold changes with runtime eligibility and selection. All four manuals correctly state that an uncomputable binding alone does not refuse a clean base. The full English scaffold difference is the instance-only Contributor Mode section.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N62\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fallback reasons and selection explanations provide actionable context. Report provenance remains the accepted low-priority F2 defect.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N63\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Mapped R1-R10 to code and focused tests. Direct R7 provenance parsing passed, while the additional end-to-end delivery-consumer assurance remains the owned F1 follow-up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The runtime paths, tests, help, manuals and ADR implement the approved carry scope. The unavailable-binding change matches current R2. The delivery declaration identifies the production validate entrypoint, and surface-check found one target with zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/adversarial-corpus\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined revision confinement before Git calls, dependency containment, physical aliases, symlinks, hidden index flags, submodules and administrative exclusions. Focused negative tests passed. Carry retains the existing local validation-record trust boundary and introduces no external execution authority.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing changed-scope selection and comparing the whole matrix and engine is smaller than per-command caching or arbitrary input hashing. Refusing every unavailable binding would disable legitimate reuse without strengthening the independent material_clean witness. This choice becomes insufficient when checks depend on undeclared inputs outside the selection model.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict --from dec2e64c1395fafbf8e2a78171e5437c1720bbbf --to 481d36dfd2ea673b5f5dc58a76d3e4213dac35bf --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran the required default command and an additional reconciliation pinned to the sealed range because automatic attribution selected a wider range. The explicit-range command exited 0; all 985 findings were warnings. Reviewed the requested source diff independently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-c1f08e237f8792fa\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not rerun the writing assessment in the sealed checkout. Examined the spec, ADR and structural change directly and used the supplied sealed design evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Skipped assessment writes under the no-change boundary. Inspected the component and independently ran focused tests; these are not represented as a new discovery assessment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Skipped the writing assessment. Traced the validation producer and delivery consumer and passed the direct carried-head parser test. Dedicated end-to-end coverage remains N63.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Skipped the writing assessment. Manually scanned the changed implementation for TODO, FIXME, stub and panic markers and checked the spec's owned follow-ups; no additional marker debt was established.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion requires POSE to record and verify this review conclusion. No attestation or closeout was recorded by this reviewer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Deferred until POSE records this conclusion; it cannot validate an attestation that does not yet exist.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully and applied the selected Backend Go, security and documentation rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"ev